ed his  face  he looked like a wistful but healthy boy  this combination of sage and boy seemed  to me always apparent in mr ford  and another friend of ford's a  contemporary of his  had the following observation  henry ford has two personalities  one is diffident almost to the point of  bashfulness yet very friendly  in 10 seconds  for no apparent reason  a smile may flip from his face  and you behold a man who from the eyes  up seems as old as the pyramids  back of the boyish board is the ford who  seems to have lived for ages  to have suffered much  and to have survived from the sheer  exercise  of the will to live  once henry ford expressed a point of  view whether it be  to go with a different carburetor in the  car or to publish an anti-semitic  newspaper  or to decide that his his mansion on the  banks of the river rouge river was going  to cost three million dollars and was  going to be built only with limestone  from one particular quarry in indiana  and that was it he was set  and no one could change his mind on  anything  and i think you have to understand that  about his personality to see how he  could develop the motivation to publish  a newspaper called the dearborn  independent the first  91 issues of which  were predominantly devoted to editorial  writings against the jews  in fact the dearborn independent  which henry ford took over it was a  failing country newspaper with a  circulation of several hundred and he  made it into this  uh  dynamic anti-jewish right-wing  publication almost instantly  its main purpose was to promulgate the  protocols of the elders of zion i don't  know how many of you are familiar with  the protocols of the elders of zion but  they are  a forgery which attribute the jewish  motivation to taking over to world  domination essentially and henry ford  was the  first  publisher of the protocols of the elders  of zion in this country and he  serialized them in his newspaper  if you take a look at  at ford's  jew at an anti-